The ST7789 display driver running at a 320x240 resolution is actually quite sharp for its physical size! At this resolution, a 16x16 pixel icon is tiny but perfectly readable if you use high-contrast, pure-color shapes without anti-aliasing.
For ST7789 displays, icons are typically uploaded directly into microcontroller firmware (like Arduino, ESP32, or Raspberry Pi Pico) as a C array hexadecimal bitmap. Since the ST7789 natively uses RGB565 (16-bit color), you can make these icons 1-bit monochome (saving RAM) and let your graphics library assign the foreground and background colors dynamically.
Here are the optimal 16x16 pixel grid mappings and ready-to-use C code bitmaps for both icons.
