## Design Notes for Low-Res Layouts

* Anti-Aliasing: If your hardware display supports color/grayscale gradients, using half-opacity pixels on corners will soften the harsh blocks. For absolute raw screens (like OLED/LCD matrices or microcontrollers), stick strictly to binary on/off.
* Padding: Each layout preserves a minimal 1-2 pixel margin buffer to prevent icons from visually bleeding into adjacent text characters or neighboring UI containers.

